.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Indirect spin-spin coupling carried through the bonding electrons (Ramsey and Purcell, 1952) splits an NMR resonance into a multiplet. The splitting is J Hz regardless of field strength. In the first-order limit, n equivalent spin-1/2 neighbours give n+1 lines with Pascal&#x27;s-triangle intensities. This example simulates ethanol&#x27;s -CH3 triplet and -CH2- quartet, then a doublet of triplets from two inequivalent coupling partners with different J values.">

